To sum up.
1) 'cu' is a part of Lojban that is not going away and that needs to be learned 
even if only for reading things from yore.
2) 'cu' is more efficient and more informative than mere terminators in the 
place where it occurs
3) It is arguable that learning 'cu' before the terminators decreases the 
students' understanding of terminators, or, at least makes them harder to learn.
4) It is arguable that learning 'cu' first has no significant effect on student 
competence with terminators nor in their ease of learning.. (the null)
5) There is presently no way to test 3 (and 4)
6) Until there is (and maybe even after), people will use whatever method they 
are comfortable with and have found successful.

BTW xorlo is not the worst thing to happen to Lojban (it is, after all 90% 
right, or better).  The worst thing to happen to Lojban is the mass of RHE, 
elidable until you need them but disastrous if you don't see you need them or 
make a mistake in using them.  I really do wish Lojban were really based on 
Symbolic Logic -- sometimes.


      

